From 0e69bcbbec06f6ffbfe11c030be8e8bc34de071f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 12:57:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(thumbnails): creative-thumbnail proxy 403'd every ad in a
 per-event ad account
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Top Creatives tiles rendered as blank initials placeholders even
after creative hydration was fixed. Hydration was not the problem —
production logs show it fully healthy:

  creative_batch_done event=NX26-DJEZ distinct_creatives=21 hydrated=84
    missing=0 no_thumbnail=0

Every creative resolved a thumbnail URL. What failed was the image
request that follows:

  GET /api/proxy/creative-thumbnail 403   (x4, every card, every load)

The proxy resolves the client's ad account from `clients.meta_ad_account_id`
alone, then calls `verifyAdAccountForThumbnail` to confirm the requested
ad belongs to it. But a client is not one ad account — that column is the
DEFAULT and `events.meta_ad_account_id` overrides it per event. Electric
Brixton's default is ELECTRIC STUDIOS SHEFFIELD (1073273492854557) while
the four NX Newcastle shows run in NX Promoter (606252931141334), so
every NX thumbnail failed the check and returned 403. The dashboard
renders that as an initials tile, which looks exactly like "Meta has no
thumbnail for this ad".

This is the same root cause as PRs #772-#776, in a surface that sweep
missed: those fixed the DATA path (which spend and creative metadata to
read), this is the IMAGE path (whether the resulting ad id may be
fetched). Both read the ad account; only one was migrated. The warm
path was already correct — it receives an event-resolved account from
the rollup-sync route, which is why `[warm-creative-thumbnails] cached
14/14` succeeds while the viewer 403s on the same ads.

Resolves the allowed set as client default UNION every distinct
`events.meta_ad_account_id` for that client, and matches the ad against
any of them. The security boundary is unchanged: ownership is still
proven by session or share token BEFORE the set is assembled, and the
set only ever contains accounts that client's own rows point at.
Widening one id to that client's real id set closes a false negative,
it does not relax a check — an unrelated account is still rejected, and
an empty or all-blank set still rejects everything rather than
degrading into a rubber stamp.

Extracts the matcher into lib/meta/ad-account-match.ts so it is
testable: thumbnail-proxy-server.ts carries `import "server-only"` and
cannot be loaded by the strip-types test runner. Same seam as
lib/meta/retry.ts. verifyAdAccountForThumbnail keeps its single-id
signature as a thin wrapper, so the warm caller is untouched.

Tests: 6, including the real Electric Brixton account pair, that an
unrelated account is still rejected, and that an empty allowed set
rejects rather than permits. Full lib suite: 51 failures before and
after, all pre-existing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
